    "Hand-reviewed mapping from the place named in each theft report to a campus rack zone.",
    "Used by backend/processing/thefts.py. Each incident's location text (or its alert text, when the location is blank) is matched case-insensitively against `match`, first entry wins.",
    "Campus buildings were looked up by name on OpenStreetMap (Nominatim, Sept 2026) and assigned to the nearest zone in data/raw/bike_theft_tracker/zones.json. The tracker's own zone matching is not used: it geocoded street addresses, and several resolved to the middle of a street (every 400-block Spence St address landed at one point ~600 m from Evans Library).",
    "Off-campus places get their own point and have no TAMU rack capacity.",
    "`unresolved` lists places that couldn't be located confidently; their incidents stay in the data but are not placed on the map. An incident that matches nothing here is an error, so newly imported reports get reviewed."
